"""
date_archive_artifacts.py

Conservative date/provenance scanner for the SAT main archive.

Purpose
-------
Main-archive files are heterogeneous: ChatGPT JSON exports, pasted transcripts,
notes, Markdown, generated summaries, PDFs, and files whose only reliable date
is when they entered Git. This tool does NOT treat every detected date as a
creation date.

It inventories date evidence and writes an auditable manifest. Renaming is
optional and deliberately conservative.

Evidence classes
----------------
1. conversation_message_range
   Native ChatGPT JSON message timestamps; strongest automatic evidence for
   conversation span.

2. explicit_content_date
   Dates parsed from text/Markdown content. These may be message dates, section
   dates, pasted source dates, or references, so they are evidence rather than
   automatically "document creation dates."

3. filename_date
   Existing date notation in the filename.

4. git_first_added
   Earliest Git commit in which the path appears. This is an ARCHIVE/LOGGING
   date unless independently corroborated; it is never silently promoted to a
   content-creation date.

5. filesystem_mtime
   Fallback only when Git history is unavailable. Weak evidence.

Default behavior
----------------
Dry-run inventory only. Produces JSONL + CSV manifests and does not rename files.

